# Files Docker must NOT send to the build context (P0.4, ahead of P12.1).
#
# `docker build` uploads this directory to the Docker daemon, and any
# `COPY . .` in a Dockerfile copies it into an image layer. Anything listed
# here is never uploaded, so it can never end up inside an image, even by
# mistake. Images can be pulled and inspected by anyone with access to them.

# --- Secrets (pitfall 16): never in an image. Secrets are given at runtime. ---
.env
.env.*
# The template has placeholders only, so it is safe to include.
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Version control: large, and could hold secrets in old commits ---
.git
.gitignore

# --- Dependencies and build output: the Dockerfile reinstalls/rebuilds these
# inside the container, so local copies (built for this OS) must not leak in ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
packages/db/generated

# --- Local tooling, logs, editor and OS files ---
*.log
*.cpuprofile
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# --- Docker files themselves (not needed inside the image) ---
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
